{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>come at the appointed season</b> — that they would come at the festivals. And it seems best to me that it is the Temple, and it is called מועד because all Israel assembles there, and likewise: 'in the midst of your מועד' (Numbers 16:3), 'they burned all the מועדי El in the land' (Lamentations 2:6)." "<b>desolate (fem.)</b> — nun in place of mem, and likewise: 'take for yourself wheat (חטין)' (Ezekiel 4:9), 'at the end of days (הימין)' (Daniel 12:13). For the nun and the mem serve at the end of a word as a sign of masculine and feminine plural." "<b>mourn</b> — from the nifal binyan, and likewise: 'mourners of the מועד' (Lamentations 1:4), which are from the root 'mourning (תוגה)' and 'grief (יגון).' The tav and the nun are added."], :book :lamentations, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Lamentations -- Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%9E%D7%92%D7%99%D7%9C%D7%AA_%D7%90%D7%99%D7%9B%D7%94"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:07:24.362929748Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}